    "result": "Perfect! The bug is now fixed. Here's a summary of what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n## Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow because the `--ci` flag was being lost when the `frai` CLI delegated to `frai-gate`.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `gate` command handler in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` was only passing positional arguments to the `frai-gate` CLI. When Commander.js parsed `frai gate init --ci`, it captured `init` as a positional argument in the `args` parameter, but the `--ci` flag wasn't being included because of how unknown options were handled with the variadic `[args...]` syntax.\n\n## Solution\nInstead of relying on Commander.js to parse the arguments, I changed the implementation to directly extract all arguments from `process.argv`:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst allArgs = process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1);\n```\n\nThis ensures all arguments and flags (like `--ci`) that come after the `gate` command are passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n## Verification\nRebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and confirmed that running `frai gate init --ci` now successfully creates both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713",
